Looking at `xarray/core/treenode.py`, `group_subtrees` iterates over subtrees grouped by relative paths. If the trees are not isomorphic, it raises `TreeIsomorphismError`.

The `prune` method should probably do something similar to `group_subtrees` but instead of raising an error when children don't match, it should only keep the children that exist in both trees.

